tr>\r\n<tr style=\"mso-yfti-irow: 3; page-break-inside: avoid;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 132.95pt; background: #DAEEF3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"177\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><span style=\"mso-bookmark: _Hlk210079572;\"><strong><span style=\"color: black; mso-color-alt: windowtext;\">Associated malignant tumours</span></strong></span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 135.9pt; background: #DAEEF3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"181\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><span style=\"mso-bookmark: _Hlk210079572;\"><span style=\"color: black; mso-color-alt: windowtext;\">Colorectal cancer, endometrial cancer, ovarian cancer, medulloblastoma</span></span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 133.55pt; background: #DAEEF3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"178\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><span style=\"mso-bookmark: _Hlk210079572;\"><span style=\"color: black; mso-color-alt: windowtext;\">Colorectal adenocarcinoma</span></span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 133.9pt; background: #DAEEF3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"179\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><span style=\"mso-bookmark: _Hlk210079572;\"><span style=\"color: black; mso-color-alt: windowtext;\">Colorectal adenocarcinoma and other GI tract cancers, breast and gynaecological tract cancers, basal cell carcinoma and sebaceous carcinoma, bladder urothelial cancer, haematological malignancies</span></span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 161.6pt; background: #DAEEF3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"215\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><span style=\"mso-bookmark: _Hlk210079572;\"><span style=\"color: black; mso-color-alt: windowtext;\">Colorectal cancer, duodenal cancer, gastric cancer, and early-onset astrocytoma (EMAST+ tumours)</span></span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"mso-yfti-irow: 4; page-break-inside: avoid;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 132.95pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"177\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><span style=\"mso-bookmark: _Hlk210079572;\"><stro